// seraphhorizons' GearConsumers switch (README.md, GearConsumers.cs; #473): the rusty gear is salvage
// and money, so every recipe that took one takes the pack's stainless gear (seraphhorizons:gear-stainless),
// in the same number (counts below are per recipe, all slots). tools/tests/test_gear_consumers.py
// holds this file to the mod's recipes.
// Pipes and Power Expanded (ppex 0.7.1). Each machine and valve has two recipes, one taking
// game:gear-rusty and one ppex:gear-* (its anvil gears): the first takes the stainless gear, the second
// is switched off. machines.json: Cornish engine 4 (/4, /9), Watt engine 2 (/5, /10), fluid pump 1
// (/6, /11), manual fluid pump 2 (/7, /12), mechanical power generator 4 (/8, /13); pipes.json:
// valve 2 (/7, /9), pressure valve 4 (/8, /10). Its anvil gears and large gears are not made any
// more (smithing/gear.json, largegear.json switched off) and are hidden from the creative inventory
// and the handbook (server side: the client gets the items from it). Large gears are only cut on
// the gear cutter (#480); smex's Bessemer converter takes the stainless large gear (GearConsumers.cs).
[
